  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt a strict 24-hour incident reporting and customer notice regime (S1), but weaken thermal testing with an 8% failure cap (vs. 5% safe) and no transition (S2). Remote shut-off is delayed to 24 months for new units and 6 years for retrofits (S3), fire suppression is required at 36 months (S4, acceptable), and the recall trigger is raised to 10/100k with corrective action at 8/100k (S5)."
 },
